Fillets: a rounding over a narrow face whose far edge is a concave crease,
the face beyond cutting the blend's side on the narrow face and growing up
to it (mitcad#343).

The case: a key's top edge rounded with 2 where the key's side B, a strip
between the edge and a bore's wall C (a torus) across a concave crease, is
2.2 high in the middle and narrower than the ball towards both ends, where
B and C end at the roundings of 0.5 of the key's end (C2). Past the
crossing where the ball's contact on B reaches the crease, the ball rolled
on the crease (patch 0011's obstacle): a ball touching the key's top and
the crease, which sticks out of the key's side, and the corners at the
ends, of four edges, failed ("Failed to find edge"). The file's rounding
keeps to B's plane all along: its cylinder, cut where C's wall runs
through it; C grows over the strip up to that cut, and at each end the
second face beyond B (C2, the end rounding) cuts the blend from where the
junction of C and C2, run on along its own circle, meets it, down to the
key's top.

ChamferOverNarrowFace (patch 0531) now also takes a rounding: where a
rounding's piece rolls on a concave crease of a face of its edges with the
face beyond, or a piece's contact ends on such a crease away from the
spine's end vertices while its other contact goes on, the rounding is
computed again with that face's surface unbounded (only across a concave
crease: over a convex one the ball rolls on the edge, patch 0620) and cut
by the faces beyond, as before where that fails. ChamferCutByFacesBeyond
takes a crossing whose other contact lies outside C's material while the
contact on B's surface past it lies inside (a rounding only): C then cuts
B's side of the blend from the crossing on, up to where the other contact
enters C's material (K), where the piece ends in a point; the piece's
contact on B ends on B's edge at the crossing (ChFi3d_NarrowCutPiece,
DegAtK). At the spine's ends, where two faces lie beyond B, the junction
of C and C2 is run on along its own curve where that is a circle, a line
or an ellipse lying on both faces (ChFi3d_EdgeRunOn; else their
intersection line); where it meets the blend before K (at Q), C cuts the
blend up to Q and C2 from Q on to the other contact, C2 growing up to the
other face from there. Where the run-on meets the other face first, it
bounds the growth instead of the edge's tangent line (ChFi3d_RunOnToFace);
where the other face and C2 meet in an edge at the spine's end vertex
through that point, the edge is cut there instead of a curve of theirs
being added. A curve of two faces the intersection lines miss at a vertex
where they touch is found by points (ChFi3d_FacesCurveByPoints), and the
curves on the faces beyond are moved into the periods of the faces' own
(ChFi3d_IntoPeriodOfFace).

On the design's stored body before the item: valid, every face of the
result on the file's within 1e-3 mm, the file's sliver of B (0.0024 mm2)
at one end 0.017 mm off ours, the change of volume -9.5996 against the
file's -9.5954 mm3; before, two corners failed. Synthetic: a key in a
spherical hollow, its top edge rounded with 2, the material taken off the
corner outside the rounding's cylinder inside the hollow within 1e-6 mm3,
with and without end walls; with them the rounding was invalid before.

Upstream: new.
